<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-CSL shares soar after H1 profit.</title>
<headline>RTRS-CSL shares soar after H1 profit.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in vaccine and blood products manufacturer, CSL Ltd, soared 4.5 percent to an intraday high of A$6.05 after reporting a 35 percent higher half year net profit of A$12.45 million, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;They are a good solid performer and have turned in a strong result this morning,&quot; said a Sydney-based dealer.</p>
<p>The company cautioned though, that full year grwoth would be lower than that achieved in the first half.</p>
<p>By 1.15 p.m. (0215 GMT), CSL shares were 21 cents higher at A$6.00 on turnover of 201,699 shares.</p>
<p>--Walter Watson 61-2 9373 1810</p>
